WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.958
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:08.340
Most rivers, when you
get to a calm section,

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:11.660
you can rest a little bit.

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:14.780
But on Murch, that
calm, flat water

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:18.260
is definitely more terrifying
than any of the white water.

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:28.780
MAN: Being a kayaker in
Central Africa, inevitably,

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:31.325
you're going to have
crocs in the river.

00:00:31.325 --> 00:00:33.700
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.500
Nile crocodiles are huge.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:44.520
They can be up to 20 feet
long, and they'll hunt you.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:49.940
They often hide under
water, waiting to strike.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:54.775
And if a crocodile attacks you,
there's nothing you can do.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:01.090
We were much more likely to
see a crocodile in a very, very

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:03.643
flat river with no current.

00:01:03.643 --> 00:01:05.935
So this is the start of
what we call the supermarket.

00:01:05.935 --> 00:01:07.030
It's very narrow.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:08.260
The water's flowing slowly.

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:11.530
Lots of rocks for
the crocs to bake on.

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:12.520
So this is-- yeah.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:15.010
I don't think I've ever gone
through here without a charge.

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:17.320
So hopefully, today
will be the first time.

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:20.570
But keep your eyes open,
guys, and scan at river level,

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:22.600
especially for,
like, open rocks.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.750
It's normally where
they hang out.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:28.090
MAN: So the supermarket
is where the crocs

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:31.210
hang out in order to feed.

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:33.310
You're the food in
their supermarket.

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:36.390
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:38.550
The risk of the
crocodile isn't when it's

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:40.260
sitting on the bank in the sun.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:46.790
The risk is when it is in the
water and you can't see it.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:59.460
Big [BLEEP] croc in this
eddy last time I was here.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.470
Definitely, the
most jaw-droppingly

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:03.330
scary experience I've ever had.

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:13.606
Henry was talking us
through the experience.

00:02:13.606 --> 00:02:17.350
We had a good
formation this morning.

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:21.430
We were able to just focus
on the sound of his voice

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:25.477
and focus on his direction in
order to not get overwhelmed.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:35.543
And all of a sudden, you
hear this glorious roar

00:02:35.543 --> 00:02:37.460
of whitewater, and you
know you're through it.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:44.215
High five, guys.

00:02:47.570 --> 00:02:51.260
But I didn't see,
like, a single croc.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:57.060
Maybe that gave a false sense
of invincibility or something.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:03:00.240
Murchison falls
definitely cemented us

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:04.500
feeling like a good solid team.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:14.580
We were ready to paddle a bunch
of rivers, explore new places,

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:18.120
and meet new people.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:21.210
That whole two months,
we were really living

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:24.345
that dream of exploration.

00:03:24.345 --> 00:03:26.112
MAN: To the best
trip ever, gentlemen.

00:03:26.112 --> 00:03:28.330
To the best trip ever.

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:31.680
[MUSIC PLAYING]

